  "content": {
    "id": "p18-p1-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "The line $y=mx-4$ is a tangent to the parabola $y=x^2-2x+5$. Find the values of $m$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=4$ or $m=-8$.",
      "worked": "At an intersection, $x^2-2x+5=mx-4$, so $x^2-(m+2)x+9=0$. Tangency gives one distinct real solution, so $\\Delta=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(m+2)^2-4(1)(9)\\\\\\Delta&=(m+2)^2-36\\\\(m+2)^2&=36\\\\m+2&=\\pm6\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence $m=4$ or $m=-8$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 26
  },
